  {
   "id": "cbd23t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 1511,
   "w": 222.0,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "context",
   "anim": {},
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "context"
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd24t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 1511,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Group work at NID tends to reward the students who think out loud.",
   "anim": {},
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd25t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 1551,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Our brief was the future of campus life at NID in 2030. We narrowed it to collaboration. Some students work things out by talking, and do well in crits and group discussions. Others work things out by making, writing or reflecting, and their contribution is easy to miss.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd26t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 1640,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Reports from UNESCO, OECD, Pew Research Center, Stanford HAI and others pointed the same way: learning environments tend to favour expressive students, attention is increasingly fragmented, and reflective learners need calmer room to work.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd27p",
   "type": "image",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 1739,
   "w": 936.0,
   "h": 468,
   "src": "projects/media/design-process/context-wall.jpg",
   "fit": "cover",
   "alt": "Sticky-note wall from early mapping sessions",
   "anim": {
    "enter": {
     "on": true,
     "from": {
      "opacity": 0,
      "y": 40
     },
     "dur": 0.9,
     "delay": 0,
     "ease": "out"
    }
   },
   "caption": "Early mapping of campus life in 2030.",
   "capShow": true
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd28t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 2371,
   "w": 222.0,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "research",
   "anim": {},
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "research"
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd29t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 2371,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "We treated expression as a spectrum, not a personality type.",
   "anim": {},
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd30t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 2411,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "We built a survey around seven scales, each with a reflective end and an expressive end, such as <em>drained ↔ energised</em> and <em>think or sketch quietly ↔ talk ideas through aloud</em>. Plotting the answers gave us seven recurring patterns, which we called learner archetypes.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd31t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 2500,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "We read these as patterns people move between, not boxes they belong in. The most common was the Ambiguous Ambivert, whose answers sit close to the middle, leaning slightly one way.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd32s",
   "type": "slides",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 2581,
   "w": 936.0,
   "h": 374,
   "fit": "contain",
   "mode": "click",
   "trans": "fade",
   "counter": true,
   "every": 3,
   "slides": [
    {
     "src": "projects/media/design-process/archetypes-1.jpg",
     "alt": "Radar charts for four learner archetypes"
    },
    {
     "src": "projects/media/design-process/archetypes-2.jpg",
     "alt": "Radar charts for three more learner archetypes"
    }
   ],
   "caption": "The seven archetypes, plotted across the seven scales. Click for the rest.",
   "capShow": true,
   "anim": {
    "enter": {
     "on": true,
     "from": {
      "opacity": 0,
      "y": 40
     },
     "dur": 0.9,
     "delay": 0,
     "ease": "out"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd33t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 3045,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Then we asked for stories.",
   "anim": {},
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd34t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 3085,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "A survey tells you what people prefer. To learn what actually happens, we ran directed storytelling sessions: students walked us through arriving at NID, getting stuck, and working in groups. We turned each conversation into an empathy map, then grouped what we heard into affinity and causal maps.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd35t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 3308,
   "w": 222.0,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "insights",
   "anim": {},
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "insights"
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd36t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 3308,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Quiet isn't the same as absent.",
   "anim": {},
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd37t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 3348,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Three findings shaped everything we made:",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd38g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3390,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 100,
   "anim": {},
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "cbd39t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "01",
     "color": "mute",
     "anim": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "cbd40t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 18,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "Quietness gets misread",
     "weight": 700,
     "anim": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "cbd41t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 52,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "Silence is often reflection or observation, not disengagement.",
     "anim": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd42g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 508,
   "y": 3390,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 100,
   "anim": {},
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "cbd43t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "02",
     "color": "mute",
     "anim": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "cbd44t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 18,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "Visible isn't the same as contributing",
     "weight": 700,
     "anim": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "cbd45t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 52,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "Making, writing and observing count, even when no one sees them happen.",
     "anim": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd46g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 746,
   "y": 3390,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 100,
   "anim": {},
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "cbd47t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "03",
     "color": "mute",
     "anim": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "cbd48t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 18,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "Feedback timing matters",
     "weight": 700,
     "anim": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "cbd49t",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 52,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 14,
     "text": "Some students want feedback right away. Others need time with an idea first.",
     "anim": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd50t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 3547,
   "w": 222.0,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "research question",
   "anim": {},
   "color": "mute"
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd51t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 3547,
   "w": 698.0,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "How do we make learning more collaborative for people with different levels of expression, at NID in 2030?",
   "anim": {},
   "weight": 700
  },
