  {
   "id": "cbd67t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32.0,
   "y": 5908,
   "w": 222.0,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "empathy game",
   "anim": {},
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "empathy game"
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd68t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 5908,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "A card game where nobody can win alone.",
   "anim": {},
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd69t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 5948,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "Players share a goal pattern that no one is allowed to describe. Each player has one kind of move, like move or rotate, and can only talk about actions. To win, they have to say a lot with a little, build a shared picture of the goal, and rely on each other's roles.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd70t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270.0,
   "y": 6037,
   "w": 539.3333333333334,
   "h": 14,
   "text": "We watched teams play and looked for three endings: the team loses because communication breaks down; the team wins but one player takes over; or the team wins and learns. Winning turned out not to mean collaborating.",
   "anim": {}
  },
  {
   "id": "cbd71p",
   "type": "image",
   "x": 270,
